I don't think that this is a viable option.  If you have seven wishes, 
you should get at least MR immediately.  Otherwise, a wand of death or a 
polymorph trap might end your game that started so micely (the latter 
might not be so bad, because you would become a green dragon).  Also 
being able to have reflection only by the amulet would not be desirable 
towards later stages of the game, therefore, if I'd opt for MR from a 
cloak, I would take silver DSM, too (unless playing a monk, of course, 
in which case green DSM would however not be an option either).  So I 
think, if you wish for DSM, it should be either gray or silver...  If 
you have a single wish at a stage of the game where you can already 
expect lichs to turn up and still haven't MR, then gray is a must. 
Earlier on, SDM is o.k., because running into a polymorph trap wearing a 
silver dragon scale mail is not too bad... (In slash'em, SDM is even 
more desirable, because you might need your amulet slot for an amulet of 
drain resistance most of the time.)

Moreover, since a corpse of a green dragon can give you poison 
resistance with certainty, you don't need the scale mail at all.  Just 
wish for the corpse or rather for a tin of it, if that works.  (I did 
not succeed wishing for a blessed tin of floating eye meat in a recent 
wizard mode test.  Don't know why, but if you can't wish for a tin, you 
should wish for the corpse.  But then make sure, you are almost hungry 
and undisturbed while eating.  You might hide in a closet...)
